---
title: Posting a tweet — from upload to follower timeline
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User (browser)
    participant W as web
    participant G as gateway
    participant T as tweet-service
    participant D as DynamoDB
    participant S3 as S3
    participant ST as DynamoDB Streams
    participant F as fanout-worker
    participant RC as redis-celeb
    participant PG as PostgreSQL (search)

    Note over U,S3: Media is uploaded directly — it never transits a pod

    U->>W: compose tweet with image
    W->>G: POST /api/v1/media/presign
    G->>T: presign request (JWT subject in header)
    T->>S3: generate presigned PUT URL
    T-->>G: { url, objectKey }
    G-->>W: { url, objectKey }
    W-->>U: presigned URL
    U->>S3: PUT image bytes (direct)

    Note over U,D: The write path — one transaction, and that transaction is the event

    U->>W: submit
    W->>G: POST /api/v1/tweets { body, objectKey, Idempotency-Key }
    G->>G: validate JWT, check rate limit, attach correlation ID
    G->>T: forward request

    rect rgb(235, 244, 255)
        Note over T,D: single TransactWriteItems
        T->>D: Put idempotency (attribute_not_exists)
        T->>D: Put tweets item
        T->>D: Update users ADD tweetCount 1
        D-->>T: committed
    end

    T-->>G: 201 Created
    G-->>W: 201 Created
    W-->>U: tweet appears optimistically

    Note over ST,PG: Asynchronous — the user is no longer waiting

    D-)ST: change record (NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES)

    par fan-out consumer
        ST-)F: GetRecords
        F->>D: GetItem users (followerCount)
        alt author has < 10,000 followers  (fan-out on write)
            loop paged over follows.gsi_followers
                F->>D: BatchWriteItem timelines (25 per call)
            end
        else author is a celebrity  (fan-out on read)
            F->>RC: SADD celebrities, LPUSH celeb:tweets
            Note right of F: no per-follower writes —<br/>timeline-service merges<br/>these tweets at read time
        end
        F->>D: checkpoint shard position
    and search indexer
        ST-)T: GetRecords
        T->>PG: upsert tweet_search + hashtags
        T->>D: checkpoint shard position
    end

    Note over F,ST: Failure is retried 3 times, then written to the deadletter<br/>table so the shard can advance. Stream retention is 24 hours —<br/>a consumer down longer than that loses records permanently.
